      heading: "How to Choose the Right Service",
      content: `<p>The best provider depends on your specific situation. Ask yourself:</p>
<p>How much are you sending? For large transfers ($3,000+), Currencies Direct or OFX offer the best value. For smaller amounts, Remitly or SoFi are more cost-effective.</p>
<p>How fast do you need it? For instant delivery, Remitly Express or OnePay Cash are your best bets. For non-urgent transfers, CurrencyFair or OFX can save you money.</p>
<p>Does your recipient have a bank account? If not, Western Union or OnePay offer cash pickup at hundreds of thousands of locations.</p>
<p>How often do you send? Regular senders benefit from CurrencyFair's free transfer offers or SoFi's flat-fee model.</p>
<p>For a personalized comparison with real-time rates, <a href="/send-money">use our comparison tool</a> — it shows the exact cost for your corridor and amount. For popular routes, check our <a href="/send-money/usa-to-india">USA to India</a> and <a href="/send-money/usa-to-philippines">USA to Philippines</a> corridor pages. For a side-by-side breakdown, see our <a href="/compare/wise-vs-remitly">Wise vs Remitly comparison</a>.</p>`,
