      heading: "How to Judge Whether a Promo Is Actually Worth It",
      content: `<p>There are four questions worth asking before you use any remittance promo:</p>
<p><strong>What is the provider's base exchange-rate spread? A weak FX rate can erase a fee discount immediately.</strong></p>
<p>Does the offer apply only to the first transfer? Many promotions are built to win the first transaction but not necessarily repeat business.</p>
<p>Does the bonus require a minimum amount or a specific funding method? Card-funded transfers sometimes trigger extra fees that blunt the discount.</p>
<p>Would you still choose the provider without the bonus? If the answer is no, the promotion probably is not creating real long-term value.</p>
<p>That framework matters most on big corridors where competition is already tight. On routes like <a href="/send-money/uk-to-india">UK to India</a> or <a href="/send-money/usa-to-mexico">USA to Mexico</a>, the "best promo" and the "best all-in transfer" are often two different providers.</p>`,
